2000000\\):\n\n\\[\n2000000(1001001 - 1001) = 2000000 \\cdot 1000000 = 2 \\cdot 10^{12}\n\\]\n\nThe rightmost non-zero digit of \\(2 \\cdot 10^{12}\\) is \\(2\\), and it is followed by \\(12\\) zeroes. Therefore, the ordered pair \\((a, b)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{(2, 12)}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{(2, 12)}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To solve the problem, we first simplify the given expression:\n\n\\[\n(1001001)(1010101) + (989899)(1001001) - (1001)(989899) - (1010101)(1001)\n\\]\n\nWe can factor the expression by grouping terms:\n\n\\[\n(1001001)(1010101) + (989899)(1001001) - (1001)(989899) - (1010101)(1001)\n= 1001001(1010101 + 989899) - 1001(989899 + 1010101)\n\\]\n\nNotice that \\(1010101 + 989899 = 2000000\\), so the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n1001001 \\cdot 2000000 - 1001 \\cdot 2000000\n\\]\n\nWe can factor out \\(2000000\\):\n\n\\[\n2000000(1001001 - 1001) = 2000000 \\cdot 1000000 = 2 \\cdot 10^{12}\n\\]\n\nThe rightmost non-zero digit of \\(2 \\cdot 10^{12}\\) is \\(2\\), and it is followed by \\(12\\) zeroes. Therefore, the ordered pair \\((a, b)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{(2, 12)}\n\\]","id":"algebra:117"}
